James needs to buy enough crepe paper to cover the perimeter of the rectangular fence. The perimeter of a rectangle is found by the formula P = 2l + 2w, where P is the perimeter, l is the length, and w is the width. In this case, the length is 20 feet and the width is 15 feet. So, the perimeter is P = 2(20) + 2(15) = 40 + 30 = 70 feet. James needs 70 feet of crepe paper.
